# Wallet seeds and endpoints for remote runs live in ONE file per network at
# the repo root, not here:
#
#   .env.preprod   see .env.preprod.example  (npm run test:preprod)
#   .env.preview   see .env.preview.example  (npm run test:preview)
#   .env.custom    see .env.custom.example   (npm run test:custom)
#
# All are gitignored. For preprod and preview, `npm run wallets:new` (with
# MIDNIGHT_NETWORK=preview for preview) writes the file for you. The local
# devnet uses its genesis seeds and reads none of them.
#
# Seeds are named per network and role, MIDNIGHT_<NETWORK>_<ROLE>_SEED, where
# ROLE is ALICE, BOB, CHARLIE or DAVE. For example:
#
#   MIDNIGHT_PREPROD_ALICE_SEED=<64 hex chars>
#   MIDNIGHT_CUSTOM_BOB_SEED=<64 hex chars>
#
# Use _MNEMONIC (24 words) in place of _SEED if you prefer. The optional
# _BIRTHDAY is written only by `npm run wallets:new`; see FAST-SYNC.md.
#
# This file, copied to .env (also gitignored), is read on EVERY remote
# network before the network's own file, so use it only for values shared by
# all of them. Shell variables override both.

# Optional: a proof server other than http://127.0.0.1:6300.
# MIDNIGHT_PROOF_SERVER=
